{"kind":"report","text":"Decision on 3c5f3a9b (planner, 2026-10-20 15:40 ET). Item 4 of 08e261c4 gains a bounded retained-copy rule. It is part of 9a and is reviewed with 9a's head.\n\n1. Membership@8 journals stay unexported, and the pin stays refused unsupported-credential-cohort.\n2. Inside an admitted directory@16, rules@10 or destination@12 journal, a retained copy of a membership@8 entry is admitted only when both checks pass:\n   a. The copied entry's kind is on an explicit list in code. The list holds only membership@8 kinds whose declared fields and effects record no secret, no digest of a secret and no private key. It never holds join or enrol (inline secret, membership.ts:385, :404), and never a kind that records an invitation hash. The builder proposes the list from the membership@8 declaration with a citation for each kind. The checker reviews it.\n   b. A check of the copy's bytes finds no field named secret.\n3. A copy that fails either check refuses the whole export, as today. No entry is skipped, redacted or rewritten; decision 4cfc2230 stands.\n4. Hosted facts for scale, read through the operator's MCP at 15:30 ET, entry kinds only and no field values: establish 0, seat 2, first-key 3, add-member 5 and 8, invite-key 6 and 9, enrol 11 and 12, and deliveries. Only an entry with sends can be retained by a consumer. Enrol 11 and 12 send nothing. The witness still runs both checks on the actual copies.\n5. Witness: the Grow fixture's three copies (directory seq 2 and 9, rules seq 7) pass both checks and the export proceeds. A constructed copy of an enrol entry, and a copy of a listed kind with a secret field added, each refuse the whole export unsupported-credential-cohort.\n6. The /grow/ line also says that the archived directory journal names the room's members as the directory recorded them.\n\nNo other widening of export, cohort or privacy permission, and no anchor beyond the one of the anchor decision on 0dcfdc62.","body":{"to":"builder"}}